---
// src/pages/house-of-prayer.astro — The House of Prayer
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import PullQuote from '../components/PullQuote.astro';
import Reveal from '../components/Reveal.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';

const prayerFocus = [
  'Firebrand Revivalists and every ministry entrusted to it, including the school chaplaincy',
  'The leaders, employees, clients, and decisions connected to the family’s marketplace work',
  'Churches, pastors, ministries, and businesses that request prayer partnership',
  'Moravian Falls, the surrounding counties, North Carolina, and the nation',
  'Every guest and family before, during, and after a stay at Ember Ridge',
];

---

<BaseLayout
  title="The House of Prayer"
  description="Before Ember Ridge ministers to people, it will minister to God. Worship, intercession, day-and-night prayer, and the spiritual foundation of the house."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="The First Ministry"
    title="A House That Ministers to the Lord"
    lede="Before Ember Ridge ministers to people, it will minister to God through worship, prayer, consecration, and attentive obedience."
  />

  <Section tone="ivory" labelledby="order-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <Reveal>
        <SectionHeading
          id="order-heading"
          eyebrow="The Order of Ministry"
          title="Public ministry flows from private communion"
        />
      </Reveal>
      <div class="mt-12">
        <Prose>
          <p>
            The deepest distinctive of Ember Ridge is not the property, the
            hospitality, or even the restoration work. It is the order of ministry.
          </p>
          <p>
            Scripture reveals the same order again and again. Isaiah calls God's house a
            house of prayer. David appointed singers to minister continually before the
            Lord. Antioch was worshiping and fasting when the Holy Spirit spoke. Jesus
            withdrew from the crowds to be alone with the Father.
          </p>
          <p>
            Anna offers the clearest pattern. Luke records that she remained in the
            temple, worshiping with fasting and prayer night and day. Hers was not a
            visible ministry. She gave herself to the Lord, and from that hidden place
            she recognised the Messiah when He appeared.
          </p>
          <p>
            There are seasons in which ministering to the Lord day and night is itself
            the assignment. Extended prayer watches, worship, fasting and waiting on God
            will become part of the life of this house.
          </p>
        </Prose>

        <PullQuote feature cite="Ember Ridge Founding Vision">
          We believe the greatest movements of God have never been sustained by gifted
          personalities alone, but by hidden men and women who first ministered to the
          Lord.
        </PullQuote>

        <Prose>
          <p>
            Church history confirms the same pattern. The Moravian prayer watch at
            Herrnhut continued for more than a century and helped fuel a missionary
            movement whose influence reached nations.
          </p>
          <p>
            The names of intercessors are less remembered than the names of speakers.
            Their service before God has shaped history all the same.
          </p>
        </Prose>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="linen" id="intercession" labelledby="intercession-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <Reveal>
        <SectionHeading
          id="intercession-heading"
          eyebrow="Intercession"
          title="Prayer at the foundation"
          lede="Intercession is not a department at Ember Ridge. It is part of how the house was conceived, and part of how it will stand."
        />
      </Reveal>

      <div class="mt-14 grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">
        <div class="lg:col-span-7">
          <Reveal class="prose-body">
            <p>
              A dedicated team gives itself to sustained prayer for this work — for the
              ministries entrusted to Firebrand Revivalists, for the churches and leaders
              who ask for it, for this region, and for every guest who comes to the
              mountain, before they arrive and long after they leave.
            </p>
            <p>
              These intercessors partner with leadership rather than direct it. They
              receive prayer focuses and carry them faithfully; what they sense is
              offered back with humility, to be weighed in Scripture and counsel. Their
              service is spiritual support, not governance — and that clarity is what
              allows them to pray freely.
            </p>
            <p>
              Confidentiality is assumed. Alignment with Scripture and with the vision
              of the house is expected. Where the ministry provides compensation for
              those called into sustained service, it honors the hours, discipline, and
              discretion that such prayer requires — never the outcome of the prayer
              itself.
            </p>
          </Reveal>
        </div>

        <aside class="lg:col-span-5">
          <Reveal delay={120} class="glass p-8 sm:p-9">
            <h3 class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-gold-700">
              Carried in prayer
            </h3>
            <div class="brushed-gold mt-5 h-px w-14"></div>
            <ul class="mt-7 space-y-4">
              {prayerFocus.map((item) => (
                <li class="flex items-start gap-4">
                  <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2.5 h-1 w-1 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-gold-500"></span>
                  <span class="text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-ink">{item}</span>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </Reveal>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="cream">
    <div class="shell">
      <Reveal class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
        <p class="eyebrow">An Invitation</p>
        <p class="display-3 mt-5">If God is inviting you to pray with us, there is a place for you here.</p>
        <div class="brushed-gold mx-auto mt-8 h-px w-20"></div>
        <p class="mt-10">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn-gold">Pray with us</a>
        </p>
      </Reveal>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <CTASection
    eyebrow="Intercession"
    title="Stand with us in prayer"
    body="Intercessors receive prayer focuses from leadership and carry them faithfully. If you sense the Lord drawing you into that, we would be glad to know."
    primary={{ label: 'Join the intercession', href: '/contact' }}
    secondary={{ label: 'How the ministry works', href: '/ministry-model' }}
  />
</BaseLayout>
